    {
      "text": "angels came and ministered unto him, Matt. 4:11. she arose, and ministered unto them, Matt. 8:15. great among you, let him be your minister, Matt. 20:26. Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, Matt. 20:28. when saw we thee … and did not minister unto thee, Matt. 25:44. eyewitnesses, and ministers of the word, Luke 1:2. they ministered to the Lord, and fasted, Acts 13:2. they had also John to their minister, Acts 13:5. these hands have ministered unto my necessities, Acts 20:34. I have appeared … to make thee a minister and a witness, Acts 26:16. I should be the minister … to the Gentiles, Rom. 15:16. I go unto Jerusalem to minister unto the saints, Rom. 15:25. ministers by whom ye believed, 1 Cor. 3:5. so account of us, as of the ministers of Christ, 1 Cor. 4:1. they which minister about holy things live of the things, 1 Cor. 9:13. made us able ministers of the new testament, 2 Cor. 3:6. approving ourselves as the ministers of God, 2 Cor. 6:4. Are they ministers of Christ, 2 Cor. 11:23. Christ the minister of sin? God forbid, Gal. 2:17. He therefore that ministereth to you the Spirit, Gal. 3:5. minister grace unto the hearers, Eph. 4:29. beloved brother and faithful minister in the Lord, Eph. 6:21. the gospel … whereof I Paul am made a minister, Col. 1:23. thou shalt be a good minister of Jesus Christ, 1 Tim. 4:6. ye have ministered to the saints, and do minister, Heb. 6:10. minister of the sanctuary … of the true tabernacle, Heb. 8:2. if any man minister, let him do it as of the ability which God giveth, 1 Pet. 4:11.",
